    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Louis Boyce Estate Agents are delighted to bring this superbly located family home to the market.This four/five bedroom spacious detached home sits on an elevated site overlooking the Ards Estuary and is beside Ards Friary, Beach, and Ards Forest Park. Creeslough (5 mins) and Dunfanaghy (10 mins).\n\nThis property has a bright open plan kitchen/dining/sunroom with good sea views and is presented in excellent condition throughout. It will appeal to a wide range of buyers seeking both residential or holiday home accommodation in a much sought after location. Extending to 2500 sq ft, the accommodation is well-proportioned and designed. \n\nA Spacious Family Home in a Beautiful Donegal Setting\n\nSet on an elevated 0.42-acre site overlooking Ards Estuary, with direct access to Ards Forest Park, this home enjoys a setting that`s hard to beat.\n\nInside, there`s a wonderful sense of space and light. The ground floor centres around a generous open-plan kitchen, living and dining area, complemented by a large second living room running the length of the house, with windows to the front and side and French doors opening to the rear.\n\nThere are four generous double bedrooms in total, including three with their own en-suites. A separate room off the main bedroom offers great flexibility as a home office, nursery, dressing room or gym. A main bathroom, utility room, walk-in cupboard and extensive eaves storage add plenty of practicality for everyday family life.\n\nOutside, the south-facing gardens enjoy sunshine throughout the day, while the fully enclosed rear garden provides a private and peaceful space for children, pets or entertaining. To the front, a stone driveway offers ample parking, with paved areas and an extensive lawn completing the grounds.\n\nProperty Highlights\n\n* Elevated site of approximately 0.42 acres\n* Overlooking Ards Estuary\n* Direct access to Ards Forest Park\n* Four generous double bedrooms\n* Three en-suite bedrooms\n* Additional home office/nursery/gym space\n* Large open-plan kitchen/living/dining area\n* Spacious second living room\n* South-facing gardens\n* Private, fully enclosed rear garden\n* Excellent storage throughout\n* Ample off-street parking\n\nA spacious, welcoming home combining privacy, practicality and an exceptional location, with the outdoors quite literally on your doorstep.\n\nThis is a property that needs to be experienced in person to fully appreciate the space, layout and setting. Contact Louis Boyce Estate Agents today to arrange your viewing and come see what this home has to offer.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hallway - 25'0\" (7.62m) x 7'3\" (2.21m)\nSpacious hallway\nSolid wooden flooring\nPine staircase\n\n\nKitchen/Dining area - 15'8\" (4.78m) x 13'9\" (4.19m)\nSolid wooden flooring\nSolid oak eye and low level units w, stainless steel sink.\nOven & gas hob.\n\n\nLiving room - 15'9\" (4.8m) x 13'9\" (4.19m)\nSolid wooden flooring\nStone surround open fireplace\nBeautiful sea views\n\nSunroom - 26'2\" (7.98m) x 15'5\" (4.7m)\nSolid wooden flooring\nStone surround open fireplace\nBeautiful sea views\nDouble pvc doors to rear\n\nUtility room\nTiled flooring\n\nBedroom 1 - 15'9\" (4.8m) x 15'1\" (4.6m)\nWooden flooring\nEnsuite tiled floor\nPartially tiled walls\nWc Whb, & shower\n\nBedroom 2 - 13'2\" (4.01m) x 11'2\" (3.4m)\nWooden flooring\n\n\nBathroom - 9'0\" (2.74m) x 6'7\" (2.01m)\nTiled flooring and partially tiled walls\nWc, Whb, & shower.\n\nBedroom 3 upstairs - 19'9\" (6.02m) x 16'5\" (5m)\nWooden flooring\nEnsuite tiled floor\nPartially tiled walls\nWc Whb, & shower\n\nOffice/study/dressing room - 16'5\" (5m) x 12'0\" (3.66m)\nSituated off the main bedroom\nWooden flooring\n\nBedroom 4\nWooden flooring\nEnsuite tiled floor\nPartially tiled walls\nWc Whb, & shower\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
